 "what": "Check of experiment-repo fbdb6f3 (code/baselines/vit_mu.py, results/e7/dev/vit_mu_e3.json): the arXiv 2610.02344\nmu baseline for the ViT, against the paper's own definitions, on the same E3 rows as code/checks/e7_dev_vit_mu.py.\n\nPaper (v1): Eq. (31) singular-value form mu~_kl = [sv_k(Sigma_X1)/a_k] * [sv_l(Wp^T M2bar)/p_l], gamma~_kl paired with\na_k p_l of the SAME (k, l) (App. A.4 warns that pairing the k-th largest gamma with the k-th largest sigma miscounts);\nU~ = {(k,l): mu~_kl > 1}; rank budget r~_tight = min(|pi_k U~|, |pi_l U~|, d, N) (Cor. 3.3, Prop. C.4, Table 7); J.1\nweight decay as an additive floor, escape iff gamma - sigma > eta.  The data and predictor factors are taken exactly as\nvit_mu.py computes them (data_k = sv_k(p S)/eig_k(S11), pred_l = (1-p) s_l / s_l^2); only the pairing, the count and\nthe floor's units differ.  Units: vit_jepa.py trains on F.mse_loss (mean over batch x target tokens x width d), whose\ngradient is (2/d) times that of the paper's 1/2 E||.||^2, so in the run's own step units the floor reads\n(2/d) g (gamma - sigma) > wd, g = 1/(1-momentum); vit_mu.py uses g (gamma - sigma) > wd.\nUsage: python3 e7_vit_mu_check.py EXP_TREE DATA_DIR OUT.json\n",
